# AlphaMind scheduler -- times are in America/New_York (see Dockerfile's TZ),
# so these stay correct across DST changes automatically.
#
# Holidays: cron only knows weekdays (`1-5`); the NYSE
# calendar (weekends, market holidays such as Thanksgiving, Christmas,
# July 4th) is checked by the services themselves (shared/market_calendar.py,
# "today" in America/New_York). On a closed market day market-open,
# market-close (core-service) and tier-monitoring (ai-service) answer
# 200 {"skipped": true, "reason": ...} without doing any work, and
# call-job.sh logs that answer. Early-close days (13:00 close) are treated
# as normal trading days: the after-close jobs simply run later than
# needed. review-run, rag-ingest, backup, logs-cleanup, purge-unverified
# and notification-retention run every day on purpose (see their comments
# below).
#
# Output: every job writes to the container's own
# stdout/stderr (/proc/1/fd/1, /proc/1/fd/2 -- PID 1 is entrypoint.sh,
# crond's parent) instead of /var/log/scheduler.log inside the container,
# so `docker compose logs scheduler` and the `vector` collector
# (./logs/scheduler/<date>.log) capture it.

# Market open: 9:30 AM ET, Monday-Friday
30 9 * * 1-5 /scripts/call-job.sh market-open >/proc/1/fd/1 2>/proc/1/fd/2

# Market close: 5:30 PM ET, Monday-Friday.
# Recomputes every portfolio's NAV snapshot for the day. It runs AFTER
# tier monitoring (5:00 PM, below), because tier monitoring can execute
# triggered recommendation tiers into the portfolios' transaction ledger,
# and those trades must be in the day's snapshot. By 5:30 PM the provider's final end-of-day bar is also
# settled. Tier monitoring has a 900 s time limit
# (call-job.sh), so it has finished before this starts.
30 17 * * 1-5 /scripts/call-job.sh market-close >/proc/1/fd/1 2>/proc/1/fd/2

# Tier monitoring: checks every accepted (or still-acceptable) recommendation
# tier for a real trigger (today's actual high/low crossing the target price)
# or expiry (past its window) -- Workflow C phase 2/3 (the tier state
# machine is described in shared/enums.py). 5:00 PM ET, Monday-Friday only (no new price data
# on a closed market day, so nothing to check; holidays are skipped by
# ai-service itself, see the top of this file). One hour after the 4:00 PM
# market close: the data provider's final EOD bar for the day isn't
# necessarily available the instant the market closes, so this waits a
# buffer rather than racing for data that might not be settled yet.
# market-close (5:30 PM, above) runs after it.
0 17 * * 1-5 /scripts/call-job.sh tier-monitoring >/proc/1/fd/1 2>/proc/1/fd/2

# Review: AI recommendation accuracy, user decision outcomes, and agent
# metrics rollup (ai-service). Runs once daily rather than tied to market
# hours -- unlike market-open/close, nothing here is time-sensitive to
# the trading session itself (it scores recommendations once they are 30
# days old and user decisions at 7, 30 and 90 days). 2:00 AM ET: after the prior day's
# market-close processing, well before the next market-open job, on
# every day of the week (not just weekdays) since decision/recommendation
# aging doesn't pause on weekends the way market data does.
0 2 * * * /scripts/call-job.sh review-run >/proc/1/fd/1 2>/proc/1/fd/2

# RAG auto-ingestion: checks every tracked ticker (portfolio holdings +
# watchlists) for new SEC filings AND recent news, adding both to the RAG
# corpus automatically. See ai/workflows/auto_ingestion_workflow.py for
# exactly what's covered (filing/SEC EDGAR and news/NewsAPI; the same
# endpoint also runs the macro_research auto-ingestion). 3:00 AM ET: after review-run,
# every day (SEC EDGAR itself has no concept of "market closed" -- filings
# get posted any day, and checking on a day with nothing new is a harmless
# no-op, not a bug, same reasoning as market-open/close's holiday-handling
# note at the top).
0 3 * * * /scripts/call-job.sh rag-ingest >/proc/1/fd/1 2>/proc/1/fd/2

# Log retention: deletes ./logs/<service>/*.log files (written
# by the `vector` service) older than 14 days, plus empty directories.
# 4:00 AM ET daily: after rag-ingest, long before market-open; the date
# boundary of the log files is also America/New_York midnight, so every
# file it considers is closed. Needs ./logs mounted at /logs (see
# docker-compose.yaml's scheduler service).
0 4 * * * /scripts/logs-cleanup.sh >/proc/1/fd/1 2>/proc/1/fd/2

# Backups: Postgres dump + Qdrant snapshots + a copy of every object in
# the object storage (SeaweedFS, through its S3 API) + avatars into
# /backups/<YYYY-MM-DD_HHMM>/ (host ./backups), then prunes backups older
# than BACKUP_RETENTION_DAYS (default 7). 2:30 AM ET daily: between
# review-run (2:00) and rag-ingest (3:00), the quietest window -- no
# market job and no ingestion writes documents at that time. See
# docs/DISASTER_RECOVERY.md.
30 2 * * * /scripts/backup.sh >/proc/1/fd/1 2>/proc/1/fd/2

# Unverified account purge (auth-service): deletes, through the same path
# as an admin deletion (anonymized row, user.deleted event), every account
# that registered more than UNVERIFIED_ACCOUNT_RETENTION_DAYS (default 7)
# days ago, never verified its email, never signed in and has no OAuth
# link. 04:10 AM ET daily: after the backup, so a purged account is still
# in the previous night's backup.
10 4 * * * /scripts/call-job.sh purge-unverified >/proc/1/fd/1 2>/proc/1/fd/2

# Notification retention (core-service): deletes READ notifications
# created more than NOTIFICATION_READ_RETENTION_DAYS (default 90) days
# ago; unread ones are kept whatever their age. 04:20 AM ET daily.
20 4 * * * /scripts/call-job.sh notification-retention >/proc/1/fd/1 2>/proc/1/fd/2
